86,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":62.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0028474885151296555,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":95.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.0162,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Cracker Barrel Old Country Store, Inc. engages in the development and operation of the Cracker Barrel Old Country Store concept in the United States. The Cracker Barrel stores consist of restaurants with a gift shop. Its restaurants serve breakfast, lunch, and dinner, as well as dine-in, pick-up, and delivery services. The company gift shops offer various decorative and functional items, such as rocking chairs, seasonal gifts, apparel, toys, food, cookware, and various other gift items, as well as various candies, preserves, and other food items. Cracker Barrel Old Country Store, Inc. was incorporated in 1969 and is headquartered in Lebanon, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David J. Deno | President, CEO & Director | Age 67","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 74K people. Revenue per employee of $45K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $1K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $127 per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Cracker Barrel Old Country Stor is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.6B market cap on $3.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 68% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $88M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.51\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin -1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33051950799484076},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2415064.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): roic below cost of capital; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance d